; -HATCHEDIT (PT26, #973) on an ANSI37 hatch read from a DXF (input.dxf, written by hand: the two
; ANSI37 families of autocad-hatchedit.dxf, hatch B7, on a 60 x 40 polyline loop, no seed point,
; no ACAD XDATA, so its origin is 0,0). Properties with Enter everywhere but the scale, 2: the
; pattern stays ANSI37, scaled around 0,0. HPNAME is not updated with a pattern -HATCH cannot
; make (#927, [decisione] 6; #928, [decisione] 7), HPSCALE is: the next -HATCH proposes <ANSI31>
; and <2.0000>. Then Origin 10,5 on the hatch without XDATA: the XDATA is added (origin=10,5),
; and U takes it away again. 10,10 lies on the 45-degree family through 0,0, before and after
; the scale.
OPEN
input.dxf
-HATCHEDIT
10,10


2

!report
-HATCH
P


!esc
-HATCHEDIT
10,10
O
S
10,5
N
!report
U
